# =============================================================================
# Example: allow one more connect-src source (APP-OWNED, never applied as is)
# =============================================================================
# Copy this file to connect-src.conf (the .example suffix keeps it inert) and
# edit the value. The file is the BODY of a map keyed on the request path
# (see the "App extension of the policy" block in ../../csp.conf).
#
# The default policy already allows connect-src 'self' https:, so the usual
# reason to add a source is a WebSocket host (wss:) or a plain-http one. The
# value is APPENDED to the directive, so it starts with a space.
#
# Other files work the same way, one `default` per directive:
#   img-src*.conf, media-src*.conf, font-src*.conf, style-src*.conf
#   extra*.conf   whole new directives, value starts with "; " (frame-src ...)
#
# There is deliberately no script-src include: widening script execution is an
# edit of the policy itself, not an include.
# =============================================================================

default " wss://realtime.example.com";
